# WorkflowSuggesterPro — Engineering Brief

Distilled from NotebookLM fontes (`README.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `docs/REPOSITORY_AUDIT.md`, `docs/notebooklm-standing-prompts.md`). Refresh when those change (see `docs/notebooklm.md`).

## Constraints

- macOS 26+ (Tahoe) and Apple Silicon; Foundation Models require this floor
- ActivityWatch is local-only: `http://localhost:5600` with `aw-watcher-window`
- Generated automations are commented shell scripts for **human review before run** — not auto-executed
- API keys live in Keychain / env vars; never invent secrets or commit them
- No third-party SwiftPM packages — Apple frameworks only (Foundation, FoundationModels, Security, SwiftUI, AppKit)

## Current decisions

- Three targets: `WorkflowSuggesterCore` (shared), `WorkflowSuggesterPro` (CLI), `WorkflowSuggesterProApp` (SwiftUI Dock + menu bar)
- Pipeline: AW window events (14 days) → AFK filter → recurrence (≥4) → top 5 workflows → LLM → `AutomationScriptWriter`
- LLM order: on-device Apple Foundation Models, then cloud Anthropic/OpenAI fallback (`WORKFLOWSUGGESTER_FORCE_CLOUD` / `WORKFLOWSUGGESTER_PROVIDER`)
- Output path: `~/Library/Application Support/WorkflowSuggesterPro/GeneratedAutomations/`
- Persistent state is minimal: UserDefaults preferences + Keychain keys + generated scripts (no DB)

## Conventions

- Layout per `AGENTS.md`: `Sources/`, `Tests/`, `scripts/`, `docs/`, `archive/`; prefer move over copy; no new top-level folders without asking
- Build: `swift run WorkflowSuggesterPro`; GUI: `./scripts/build_and_run.sh`; tests: `swift test` (use `xattr -cr .build` if codesign detritus fails)
- Short questions → short answers; cite sources; missing figures → `n/v`

## Exclusions

- Do not treat NotebookLM as authority for live AW/API numbers
- Do not upload toolchain files (`Package.swift`), binaries, `.build/`, or `dist/` as NotebookLM fontes
- Do not invent new product scope (background daemons, App Store packaging) unless docs say so

## Known gaps (from audit — do not soft-pedal)

- AUDIT-001: tracked `dist/` binary (gitignore already lists it; stop tracking)
- AUDIT-002: no timeouts on AW / LLM `URLSession` requests
- AUDIT-003: generated scripts default `chmod 755` (prefer non-executable until user enables)
- Limited tests for LLM/JSON/script-writer paths

